    "title": "Iran, EU to Resume Nuclear Talks",
    "text": "Iran and the EU’s three major powers—France, Germany, and the UK—have agreed to relaunch nuclear talks next week. The decision comes as Europe threatens to activate the UN “snapback” sanctions mechanism if Tehran refuses to engage. Iran rejects the measure as illegitimate, while observers note growing repression at home following U.S. and Israeli strikes on nuclear sites. Analysts warn Western leaders must balance nuclear concerns with accountability for Iran’s human rights record.\nIran, EU to Resume Nuclear Talks\nThe decision comes as Europe threatens to activate the UN 'snapback' sanctions mechanism if Tehran refuses to engage.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 8/27/2025, 11:47:28 PM EDT",
